  "gst-for-transporters-complete-guide": {
    category: "Industry Insights",
    title: "GST for Transporters: Complete Compliance Guide 2026",
    coverImage: "/blog/og/gst-for-transporters-complete-guide.svg",
    date: "July 3, 2026",
    readTime: "8 min read",
    author: "LoadSaathi Team",
    authorBio: "The LoadSaathi engineering and product team builds AI-powered logistics tools for India's freight industry.",
    summary: "Transporters with annual turnover over ₹40 lakh must register for GST. Key compliance requirements include generating e-Way Bills for all inter-state movements of goods over ₹50,000, filing GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B returns monthly, and maintaining accurate trip records. Input Tax Credit on fuel remains unavailable for GST-registered transporters.",
    content: [
      "GST compliance is a critical aspect of operating a trucking business in India. With the new e-Way Bill rules effective August 1, 2026, transporters must stay on top of their compliance obligations to avoid penalties and Input Tax Credit (ITC) blockages that can severely impact cash flow.",
      "GST registration is mandatory for transporters with annual turnover exceeding ₹40 lakh (₹20 lakh for special category states). Transporters without GST registration cannot issue invoices with GSTIN, limiting their ability to service registered businesses who need input tax credit on freight charges.",
      "Key compliance requirements for 2026: generate e-Way Bills for all inter-state goods movements valued above ₹50,000, maintain accurate records of all trips including vehicle number, goods description, consignor and consignee details, file monthly GSTR-1 (outward supplies) by the 11th and GSTR-3B (summary return) by the 20th, and submit an annual GSTR-9 return.",
      "One important limitation: Input Tax Credit on fuel (petrol and diesel) is NOT available for GST-registered transporters. This means the GST paid on fuel purchases cannot be offset against GST collected on freight charges. However, ITC is available on vehicle purchases, spare parts, tires, and maintenance services.",
      "LoadSaathi helps transporters manage compliance by integrating with the e-Way Bill system and maintaining digital records of all trips. The platform automatically generates shipment documentation that supports GST compliance, reducing the administrative burden on truckers and fleet operators.",
    ],
  },
