  "shipper-tips-lower-freight-cost": {
    category: "Shipper Guide",
    title: "10 Proven Tips to Lower Your Freight Costs in India",
    coverImage: "/blog/og/shipper-tips-lower-freight-cost.svg",
    date: "June 8, 2026",
    readTime: "6 min read",
    author: "Amit Verma",
    authorBio: "Amit Verma is a supply chain consultant who helps SMEs in East India digitize their freight operations.",
    summary: "Reduce freight costs by up to 40% with these 10 strategies: use PTL for small loads, book return-load trucks, use AI price predictions, consolidate shipments, negotiate annual contracts, optimize packaging, avoid peak seasons, use digital platforms, maintain good credit scores, and plan routes efficiently.",
    content: [
      "Freight costs can make up 8-12% of the final product cost for many Indian businesses. For SMEs in East India operating on thin margins, reducing logistics expenses directly improves profitability. Here are 10 proven strategies to lower your freight costs without sacrificing service quality.",
      "1. Use PTL instead of FTL for loads under 3 tonnes. Sharing truck space can save 30-40% compared to booking an entire vehicle. 2. Book return-load trucks. Trucks heading back to their home base after delivering often offer discounted rates. 3. Use AI price predictions. LoadSaathi's Price Predictor ensures you don't overpay by showing you the fair market rate for every route. 4. Consolidate shipments. Combining multiple small loads into one larger shipment reduces per-unit costs significantly. 5. Negotiate annual contracts with truckers on your regular routes for volume discounts.",
      "6. Optimize packaging. Reduce dimensional weight by using compact, efficient packaging — smaller packages mean more goods per truck. 7. Avoid peak seasons. Freight rates spike during Diwali, Pujo, and harvest seasons. Plan shipments before or after these periods when possible. 8. Use digital platforms. LoadSaathi's transparent bidding model creates competition among truckers, driving rates down 15-20% compared to broker quotes. 9. Maintain a good credit score. Higher credit scores unlock better rates and priority matching on the platform. 10. Plan efficient routes. Avoid routing goods through congested city centers and plan multi-stop routes that minimize total distance.",
      "Start implementing these strategies today. Even adopting just 3-4 of these tips can reduce your freight costs by 15-25% — savings that go directly to your bottom line. Post your first shipment on LoadSaathi to experience transparent pricing and AI-powered savings immediately.",
    ],
  },
